course: dictionary
lesson: 11527
title: Allot: sharing out and setting time aside
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To allot something is to give a share of it to someone, so that each person gets a part. «The teacher allotted each group five minutes to talk.» Every group gets the same amount of time.
explain: You can also allot time for something, which means you set it aside on purpose. «We allotted an hour for reading.» That hour is kept for reading and nothing else. People in everyday talk would say give or share out, but allot sounds more formal, like the language of exams and maths.
explain: Look at the past form, allotted. «Each pupil was allotted three minutes.» The three minutes were given to each pupil. When you see «the allotted time», it means the time that has been given out for a task.
fact: Allot means to give a share or an amount of something to someone.
fact: Allot can also mean to set time aside for something.
fact: Allot is a verb: allot, allots, allotted, allotting.
fact: «The allotted time» means the time that has been given for a job.
fact: In everyday talk, you can say «give» or «share out» instead of allot.
exercise: «Each pupil is allotted three minutes to speak.» What does allotted mean here? | Taken away from them | Shouted loudly | Forgotten by everyone | *Given out as a share
exercise: «We allotted an hour for reading.» What did we do with the hour? | Lost it in the playground | *Set it aside for reading | Gave it to the dog | Used it to paint a wall
exercise: Which everyday word means about the same as allot? | *Give | Hide | Break | Forget
test: «The teacher allotted the class ten minutes to finish.» What did the teacher do? | Asked the class to sing | Ate ten sweets | *Gave the class ten minutes | Took ten minutes away
test: Which phrase means the time given out for a task? | Forgotten time | *The allotted time | Time for lunch | A time of rest
exam: Sam says, «Allot is a fancy word for hide.» What does allot really mean? | *Give a share or set time aside | Ask a question | Break something into pieces | Hide something away
